    {
      "jobId": "7b7e5fe8-2e0d-492a-ac1b-b3973a15a87a",
      "question": "For company news about the 12 most liquid issuers published from August 17 through August 24, 2026, how did the sentiment labels line up with the issuers' returns over the following five sessions? Describe the relationship without claiming causation.",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-01T04:26:44.758553Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-01T04:27:11.589094Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "**Sentiment‑label alignment with 5‑session forward returns (12 most‑liquid issuers, news 17 Aug – 24 Aug 2026)**\n\n| Sentiment label | News events | Mean 5‑session return | Median 5‑session return |\n|----------------|------------|----------------------|--------------------------|\n| Negative | 5 | **‑3.0 %** | **‑6.5 %** |\n| Neutral  | 3 | **+0.2 %** | **+3.8 %** |\n| Positive | 5 | **+3.0 %** | **+0.3 %** |\n\n*Overall sentiment‑return correlation*: **≈ 0.41** (positive), indicating that, on average, more positive news tended to be followed by higher returns over the next five trading sessions, while negative news tended to be followed by lower returns.\n\n**Key points**\n\n- The 13 aligned news events (100 % coverage) show the pattern above.\n- The correlation is modest (≈ 0.41) and **does not imply causation**; other factors (timing, market conditions, overlapping events, label quality) can influence returns.\n\n**Limitations**\n- Descriptive correlation only; not a predictive model.\n- Small sample (13 events) limits statistical confidence.\n- Results are based on synthetic market data and are not investment advice.\n\n[1]\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Market analytics result — analyze news price relationship — evidence `hermes-receipt:b14f670eff8b83daba60a1f4410cbd8fb3b52288876166eb2875df21e3815a0c`",
